title: What is Art Anyway?
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Interesting question right? how do we define art? I know my "[[Practice]]" is yes, "[[design|Design]]" but I would also say that I am an [[artist|Artist]]; is design art? is art sometimes design? is just having the right conversation in the right place art? is this just a question since [[Modernity]]?

I keep collecting answers and not settling on one: [[What Is Art Anyway? on Are.na|https://www.are.na/kristian-bjornard/what-is-art-anyway]] (142 blocks, started April 2020).

Some of what is in there:

* A garden: Piet Oudolf's planting
* A receipt for empty space: Yves Klein's //Zone de Sensibilité Picturale Immatérielle//
* A playground that was never built: Noguchi's //Play Mountain//
* Bob Ross paintings, and where they all went
* MSCHF
* James Turrell, Tania Bruguera, Mark Bradford
* A Bauhaus wall hanging
* One line of text: "The history of art has to also be a history of art education"

See [[Artist]], [[Designer]], [[Mingei]], [[BauHaus]], [[Sol LeWitt]], [[Agnes Denes]]
